<title>USA: Smith Barney shifts fund to &quot;socially responsible&quot;.</title>
<headline>Smith Barney shifts fund to &quot;socially responsible&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Smith Barney said Friday its Strategic Investors Fund has become a &quot;socially responsible&quot; fund, with the name changed to the Concert Social Awareness Fund.</p>
<p>The $380 million fund will keep its balanced strategy, and will shift the portfolio to 75 percent stock and 25 percent fixed income from the current 53 percent stocks, 40 percent fixed income and the rest in cash, according to portfolio manager Bob Brady.</p>
